    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d238-a1">

                <pb facs="0342" n="176" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg176"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Japanese Chargé
                            d’Affaires to Minister Reinsch
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Japanese Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 3, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My dear Minister</hi>, I beg to enclose copy of the
                    note of the Chinese Minister for Foreign Affairs under date of October 5, 1913
                    as desired by Baron Hayashi on the eve of his departure from Peking in
                    compliance with your request made in the personal letter of the 29th ult. on the
                    subject of cooperation between Japanese and American capital in the development
                    of railways in Manchuria. The note being naturally of confidential character, I
                    hope that your excellency will be good enough to keep it secret.</p>
                <p>With the assurance [etc.],</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Yoshizawa</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
